[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3596518517","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/113384#issuecomment-3596518517","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/113384","id":3596518517,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7WXoR1","user":{"login":"SonicSegFault","id":81888555,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODg4NTU1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81888555?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/SonicSegFault","html_url":"https://github.com/SonicSegFault","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SonicSegFault/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SonicSegFault/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SonicSegFault/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SonicSegFault/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SonicSegFault/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SonicSegFault/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SonicSegFault/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SonicSegFault/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SonicSegFault/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-12-01T13:19:39Z","updated_at":"2025-12-01T13:19:39Z","body":"Refactored the test to remove static variables and SUBCASEs. Everything is now scoped within the test case and should work as intended. This avoids unnecessary static state and keeps the test linear and readable. \r\n\r\nI moved the Ref<ENetConnection> variables into the test case scope as discussed. I also noticed that the networking connection sometimes fails in tests (client can’t always connect to server). I’m currently investigating and working on a fix.","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3596518517/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3597520131","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/113384#issuecomment-3597520131","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/113384","id":3597520131,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7Wbc0D","user":{"login":"SonicSegFault","id":81888555,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODg4NTU1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81888555?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/SonicSegFault","html_url":"https://github.com/SonicSegFault","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SonicSegFault/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SonicSegFault/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SonicSegFault/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SonicSegFault/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SonicSegFault/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SonicSegFault/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SonicSegFault/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SonicSegFault/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SonicSegFault/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-12-01T16:28:19Z","updated_at":"2025-12-01T16:28:19Z","body":"The failing checks are due to ENet being unable to bind UDP sockets in some GitHub Actions environments. This is an environment limitation, not a regression in ENet. The skip guard ensures the test runs when binding succeeds, and skips otherwise to avoid false negatives.\r\n\r\n```\r\nif (server_host->get_local_port() == 0) {\r\n    print_line(\"Skipping ENet test: server failed to bind.\");\r\n    server_host->destroy();\r\n    return;\r\n}\r\n","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3597520131/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3597540696","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/113384#issuecomment-3597540696","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/113384","id":3597540696,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7Wbh1Y","user":{"login":"AThousandShips","id":96648715,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcK-Cw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96648715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips","html_url":"https://github.com/AThousandShips","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-12-01T16:31:24Z","updated_at":"2025-12-01T16:31:24Z","body":"The compile issue is due to specific configurations needed to build the enet code, see `modules/jsonrpc` for an example of how to configure a test with build details","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3597540696/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3622538381","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/113384#issuecomment-3622538381","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/113384","id":3622538381,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7X64yN","user":{"login":"SonicSegFault","id":81888555,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODg4NTU1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81888555?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/SonicSegFault","html_url":"https://github.com/SonicSegFault","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SonicSegFault/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SonicSegFault/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SonicSegFault/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SonicSegFault/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SonicSegFault/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SonicSegFault/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SonicSegFault/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SonicSegFault/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SonicSegFault/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-12-07T16:59:08Z","updated_at":"2025-12-07T16:59:08Z","body":"It took me a few days to track this down, but the issue with the `client->server` connection was related to how ENet buffers protocol messages to reduce traffic. As a result, the connection event may not be sent immediately; it often isn’t dispatched until the first packet is transmitted. Calling `enet_host_flush` on the client after it accepts the connection forces ENet to send the connection message to the server right away.\r\n\r\nI also realized it’s not ideal to test all functions (such as `socket_send` and `broadcast`) within the same test suite. I’ve removed those from the current tests and will explore them separately. Since ENetConnection doesn’t expose the `send()` function directly for client to server packets, those cases will need to be validated differently.\r\n","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3622538381/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]